@startuml
title FR-23 - Receive Component Expiry Notice - Activity Diagram

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam conditionStyle InsideDiamond

|Server — Inventory|
start
:Monitor component expiry using\nthe approved operating mechanism;

:Read undisposed components with\ntheir expiry data and blood bank links;

:Validate expiry data and identify\nconfirmed expired components;

if (Missing or invalid expiry data found?) then (Yes)
  :Handle the expiry-data problem\nwithout claiming confirmed expiry\nfor those records;
endif

if (Any confirmed expired components?) then (Yes)

  while (Another confirmed expired component?) is (Yes)
    :Ensure the component is unavailable\nfor allocation;

    :Create a notice identifying\nthe component and its blood bank;

    if (Notice creation succeeded?) then (Yes)
      :Make the notice accessible to\nauthorized inventory staff at that bank;

      if (Notice availability failed?) then (Yes)
        :Handle the availability failure\nwhile keeping the component unavailable;
      endif

    else (No)
      :Handle the notice creation failure\nwhile keeping the component unavailable;
    endif

  endwhile (No)

else (No)
  :Complete the check without issuing\na new expiry notice for this run;
endif

stop
@enduml